  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Test for a single mean"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "To test $H_0: \\mu = \\mu_0$ from a large sample (n > 30): $Z = \\dfrac{\\bar{x} - \\mu_0}{\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}}$, where the sample s.d. $s$ may replace an unknown $\\sigma$. Under $H_0$, $Z \\sim N(0, 1)$ approximately. Compare $|Z|$ with 1.96 (5%) or 2.58 (1%) for a two-tailed test.",
    "kn": "H₀: μ = μ₀ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಲು Z = (x̄ − μ₀)/(σ/√n); σ ತಿಳಿಯದಿದ್ದರೆ s ಬಳಸಿ. |Z| ಅನ್ನು 1.96 (5%) ಅಥವಾ 2.58 (1%) ರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋಲಿಸಿ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Z = (x̄ − μ₀)/(σ/√n)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Use s when σ is unknown (large n)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Compare |Z| with the critical value"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "To test H_0: mu = mu_0 from a large sample (n > 30): Z = dfracx-bar - mu_0sigma/rootn, where the sample s.d. s may replace an unknown sigma. Under H_0, Z sim N(0, 1) approximately. Compare |Z| with 1.96 (5%) or 2.58 (1%) for a two-tailed test.",
    "kn": "H₀: μ = μ₀ ಪರೀಕ್ಷಿಸಲು Z = (x̄ − μ₀)/(σ/√n); σ ತಿಳಿಯದಿದ್ದರೆ s ಬಳಸಿ. |Z| ಅನ್ನು 1.96 (5%) ಅಥವಾ 2.58 (1%) ರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋಲಿಸಿ."
   },
   "formula": "Z=\\frac{\\bar{x}-\\mu_0}{\\sigma/\\sqrt{n}}"
  },
