  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Test for two means"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "To test $H_0: \\mu_1 = \\mu_2$ from two independent large samples: $Z = \\dfrac{\\bar{x}_1 - \\bar{x}_2}{\\sqrt{\\sigma_1^2/n_1 + \\sigma_2^2/n_2}}$. If both populations have a common s.d. $\\sigma$, the denominator is $\\sigma\\sqrt{1/n_1 + 1/n_2}$.",
